&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI in Applications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Artificial Intelligence can be a useful tool to support your application, however, all examples and statements provided must be truthful, factually accurate and taken directly from your own experience. Where plagiarism has been identified (presenting the ideas and experiences of others, or generated by artificial intelligence, as your own) applications may be withdrawn and internal candidates may be subject to disciplinary action. Please see our&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://eur02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.civil-service-careers.gov.uk%2Fartificial-intelligence-and-recruitment%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CLynn.Tan%40dsit.gov.uk%7Ccf5d753b7f19427afc8f08de4c307014%7Ccbac700502c143ebb497e6492d1b2dd8%7C0%7C0%7C639031968075235036%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=jCrYoy62YfXN%2FLIB%2FhtHxdLGbCOgropbkZXDyQsUMC4%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;02db05e7-03ca-4ca6-bcd9-73ff8bf258f2&quot; data-auth=&quot;NotApplicable&quot; data-linkindex=&quot;1&quot;&gt;candidate guidance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;for more information on appropriate and inappropriate use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI tools in recruitment&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We may use AI tools to help our hiring team review applications, for example by summarising application materials and helping us prioritise them against the published criteria. We do not use AI tools to find information about you from other sources, including online.&amp;nbsp;People make every decision. We do not make solely automated decisions about candidates. Find out more, including your rights, in our recruitment privacy notice: https://www.aisi.gov.uk/careers/privacy-policy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Fraud Database&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;The Internal Fraud function of the Fraud, Error, Debt and Grants Function at the Cabinet Office processes details of civil servants who have been dismissed for committing internal fraud, or who would have been dismissed had they not resigned. The Cabinet Office receives the details from participating government organisations of civil servants who have been dismissed, or who would have been dismissed had they not resigned, for internal fraud. In instances such as this, civil servants are then banned for 5 years from further employment in the civil service. The Cabinet Office then processes this data and discloses a limited dataset back to DLUHC as a participating government organisations. DLUHC then carry out the pre employment checks so as to detect instances where known fraudsters are attempting to reapply for roles in the civil service. In this way, the policy is ensured and the repetition of internal fraud is prevented.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;For more information please see -&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/internal-fraud-register-privacy-notice/internal-fraud-register-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Internal Fraud Register.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Security&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Successful candidates must undergo a criminal record check and get&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/government-baseline-personnel-security-standard&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/government-baseline-personnel-security-standard&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;baseline personnel security standard (BPSS)&amp;nbsp;clearance&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;before they can be appointed. Additionally, there is a strong preference for eligibility for&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/national-security-vetting-advice-for-people-who-are-being-vetted&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/national-security-vetting-advice-for-people-who-are-being-vetted&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;counter-terrorist check (CTC)&amp;nbsp;clearance&lt;/a&gt;. Some roles may require higher levels of clearance, and we will state this by exception in the job advertisement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/vetting-explained-and-our-vetting-charter/the-vetting-charter&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/vetting-explained-and-our-vetting-charter/the-vetting-charter&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;See our vetting charter here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Nationality requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;We may be able to offer roles to applicant from &lt;strong&gt;any nationality or background&lt;/strong&gt;. As such we encourage you to apply even if you do not meet the standard &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nationality-rules&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;nationality requirements (opens in a new window).&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Working for the Civil Service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field_value&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://civilservicecommission.independent.gov.uk/code/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Civil Service Code (opens in a new window)&lt;/a&gt; sets out the standards of behaviour expected of civil servants.&amp;nbsp;The Civil Service embraces diversity and promotes equal opportunities. As such, we run a Disability Confident Scheme (DCS) for candidates with disabilities who meet the minimum selection criteria.&amp;nbsp;The Civil Service also offers a Redeployment Interview Scheme to civil servants who are at risk of redundancy, and who meet the minimum requirements for the advertised vacancy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field_value&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;The Civil Service is committed to attract, retain and invest in talent wherever it is found. To learn more please see the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/civil-service-people-plan-2024-2027/civil-service-people-plan-2024-2027-html&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Civil Service People Plan (opens in a new window)&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/civil-service-diversity-and-inclusion-strategy-2022-to-2025&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Civil Service Diversity and Inclusion Strategy (opens in a new window)&lt;/a&gt;. As part of the application process, we monitor statistics on D&amp;amp;I. You can see how we process this data here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/government-digital-service-recruitment-privacy-notice/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment privacy notice - GOV.UK&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Company Profile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;nLighten is a leading European edge data centre platform operating across key markets throughout Europe. Founded in 2021, we are redefining digital infrastructure through our vision of being Close, Coupled and Connected, bringing sustainable, highly connected data centres closer to the businesses and communities we serve. As a fast-growing company, we are helping power the future of AI, cloud and digital innovation across Europe.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Learn more about us: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nlighten.com/en/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;www.nlighten.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are seeking an experienced and highly capable &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Regional Director Construction UK &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;to take full ownership of the delivery of multiple data centre construction and capital projects across&amp;nbsp;the UK.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;This is a senior leadership role responsible for driving projects from early concept and design through construction, commissioning, and final handover to Operations. You will lead a regional team of Design and Construction Managers, working closely with senior stakeholders, internal teams, and external partners to ensure projects are delivered safely, on time, within budget, and to nLighten’s quality standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Health and safety is a core priority across all projects, and you will play a critical role in promoting continuous improvement and best practice across the regional portfolio.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Regional Leadership &amp;amp; Accountability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Own the successful delivery of all construction and capital projects across the assigned region, ensuring alignment with nLighten’s strategic objectives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Lead, develop, and performance-manage a regional team of Design and Construction Managers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Act as the senior point of accountability for project outcomes, governance, and decision-making within the region.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;End-to-End Project Delivery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Lead projects from early concept and design through construction, commissioning, and operational handover.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Ensure projects are delivered safely, on schedule, within approved budgets, and to nLighten’s quality and performance standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Maintain appropriate site presence and oversight across all active regional projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Financial Control&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Maintain full accountability for regional project budgets, forecasts, and cost performance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Ensure robust control of scope, variations, and change management to protect programme and cost certainty.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Work closely with Finance and Project Controls to provide accurate and timely reporting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Health, Safety &amp;amp; Risk Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Champion a strong health and safety culture across all regional projects, ensuring zero compromise on safety standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Proactively identify, manage, and mitigate project risks and issues, escalating where required in line with governance processes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Technical, Design &amp;amp; Commissioning Oversight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Ensure compliance with nLighten design standards, technical specifications, and regulatory requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Provide senior oversight of commissioning activities, ensuring facilities are fully tested, certified, and ready for operational use.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Stakeholder &amp;amp; Partner Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, customers, consultants, contractors, and supply chain partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Lead effective collaboration and resolve conflicting priorities to achieve successful project outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Reporting, Handover &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Provide clear, concise reporting on regional project performance, risks, and milestones to senior leadership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Ensure structured and seamless handover to Operations, including documentation, training, and acceptance sign-off.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Drive continuous improvement in delivery processes, standards, and team capability across the region.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Delivery Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Senior leadership experience delivering complex construction projects within data centre or critical infrastructure environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Proven ability to lead multiple concurrent projects and geographically dispersed, multidisciplinary teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Demonstrated success delivering projects in live operational environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Project Control&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Strong expertise in budget management, cost control, and financial reporting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Solid understanding of project scheduling, risk management, and change control.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Technical Capability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Strong technical understanding of data centre construction and critical engineering systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Engineering qualification or relevant technical trade background is desirable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Stakeholder &amp;amp; Problem-Solving Skills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Ability to influence senior stakeholders and drive effective decision-making.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Excellent problem-solving skills with a track record of resolving complex project issues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Senior Leadership Impact&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: Play a key role in shaping the growth of nLighten’s European data centre platform.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;High-Profile Projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: Lead complex, business-critical infrastructure developments across multiple countries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Collaborative Culture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: Work within a supportive, forward-thinking environment that values expertise and initiative.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;If you have the right experience and are excited about contributing to the next evolution of edge data centers, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Apply now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; and be part of our journey toward a more connected, efficient, and sustainable digital future.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Diversity &amp;amp; Inclusion Statement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;nLighten is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace, and we encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds. Even if you do not meet every requirement listed, we welcome your application. We particularly encourage women and individuals from underrepresented groups to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Burson, part of WPP, is the global communications leader built to create value for clients through reputation. With highly specialized teams, industry-leading technologies and breakthrough creative, we help brands and businesses redefine reputation as a competitive advantage so they can lead today and into the future. When you work at Burson, you are part of a global community of lifelong learners who thrive at the edge of innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP (LSE/NYSE: WPP) is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel in a single company – powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open, to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;WPP.com&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/&quot;&gt;bursonglobal.com&lt;/a&gt; and follow us on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/burson/posts/?feedView=all&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/burson.global/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More about the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Burson is building three global Influence &amp;amp; Social Centres of Excellence in the US, Singapore, and London. As part of our UK Centre of Excellence, which serves as the hub for the EMEA region, we are seeking an Associate Director, Influence to play a pivotal, hands-on role in scaling and evolving our Total Influence offer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity for a mid-to-senior influencer specialist who combines strategic vision with flawless operational execution. Sitting within our multi-disciplinary capability, you will be the day-to-day strategic engine and trusted advisor across all agency practices. You will plan, oversee, and execute best-in-class influencer-led campaigns that earn cultural relevance, protect reputation, and deliver measurable business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Influence Associate Director, you will be a dynamic, commercially astute specialist and creative thinker, leading best-in-class, influencer-led content strategies and programmes across all agency sectors. Viewing &quot;influence&quot; holistically, you will provide strategic and practical counsel to clients and internal teams; from identification, vetting, and contracting to creative co-creation, paid integration, and measurement. Partnering with UK head of Influence, you will elevate Burson’s influencer marketing offer, inspire dedicated specialists, and upskill teams to deliver exceptional, measurable results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Grow: Commercial &amp;amp; Sector Partnership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Influence Partner: Act as a trusted adviser to sector and practice leads, translating client and business briefs into culturally relevant, influencer-led strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Organic Growth: Partner with the UK Head of Influence and senior teams to develop winning pitches, shape commercial models and identify opportunities to grow influence across existing and new client accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holistic Influence Strategy: Champion a broader view of influence beyond traditional creators, incorporating thought leaders, B2B voices, subject-matter experts and advocates across owned, earned, shared and paid channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Enable: Delivery, Operations &amp;amp; Best Practice&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-Class Campaign Delivery: Lead end-to-end influencer programmes, from discovery, vetting and contracting through to creator briefing, co-creation, rights management and live campaign delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative, Paid &amp;amp; Performance Integration: Work closely with creators to deliver authentic, high-quality content while connecting organic influence with paid amplification, licensing, whitelisting and performance marketing opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Governance, Tools &amp;amp; Team Development: Ensure programmes meet ASA, CMA, IP and Burson compliance standards, while embedding tools such as CreatorIQ and GWI and upskilling teams on influencer best practice, cultural trends and effective ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Transform: Innovation &amp;amp; Modern Measurement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurement &amp;amp; Impact: Partner with data and intelligence specialists to evolve how influence is measured, moving beyond vanity metrics to demonstrate sentiment, cultural share of voice, reputation shift and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform &amp;amp; Innovation Leadership: Build strong relationships with platforms including TikTok, Meta, YouTube and LinkedIn, while testing and embedding AI and emerging capabilities through Burson&#39;s AI suite and WPP Open to improve discovery, reporting and workflow efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience that contributes to success:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven Agency Experience: Substantial influencer marketing experience within an agency, PR, or integrated creative environment, operating at Account Director / Junior Associate Director level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic &amp;amp; Creative Rigour: Ability to plan multi-channel content strategies that are influencer-first, with a strong understanding of how audience mapping and data inform creative platforms and creator selection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiation &amp;amp; Contracting Mastery: Deep practical expertise in creator negotiation, complex scope structuring, multi-platform licensing, exclusivity, and contract management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech Fluency: Hands-on proficiency with dedicated influencer tech platforms (specifically CreatorIQ) and consumer research tools (such as GWI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Leadership: A natural relationship-builder who can seamlessly partner with cross-functional teams (strategy, creative, earned media, paid, data) and mentor junior talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client Advisory Skills: Calm, authoritative client-handling skills with the ability to articulate the strategic value of influencer marketing to both senior brand marketers and communications directors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Acumen: Experience building accurate scopes of work, production budgets, talent fees, and pitch responses that protect agency margins and client ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Burson UK was named Cannes Lions Agency of the year 2026!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-CY1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You belong at Burson:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is for Burson to be the leading ‘academy company’ for creative communications professionals and emerging leaders. We provide a dynamic environment where ambitious colleagues come to elevate their skills, expand their networks, and ultimately, produce the best solutions for today’s leading brands. Our commitment to your growth is reflected in our robust benefits and people programs, which include professional development opportunities, mentorship programs with industry leaders, a vibrant and inclusive company culture fostering collaboration and innovation and packages designed to reward and retain top talent. We invest in our people because we believe their success is our success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Burson, we’re an agency of learn-it-alls. We recognize that the things we do best, creativity and communications, require a level of nuanced understanding. That’s why it’s imperative for us to hire extraordinarily talented people of all backgrounds and identities. Without that we can’t do the essential work of inspiring bold ideas, fostering constructive dialogue, cultivating meaningful experiences, and driving innovation and creativity for our partners. Your unique point of view—your talent—is what makes you a #BursonPerson, and it’s how we deliver exceptional results for our clients, together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you click the &quot;Submit Application&quot; button below, this will send any information you add below to Burson. Before you do this, we think it&#39;s a good idea to read through our &amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy. &lt;/a&gt;California residents should read our  &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice. &lt;/a&gt;This explains what we do with your personal data when you apply for a role with us, and, how you can update the information you have provided us with or how to remove it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About BakerHicks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BakerHicks is a leading design, engineering and project delivery consultancy, delivering complex infrastructure, industrial and built environment projects across the UK and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Infrastructure team supports a wide range of clients and frameworks, providing specialist engineering, inspection, surveying and asset management services. As our project portfolio continues to grow, we are expanding our network of trusted contractors to support current and future bridge inspection requirements across the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our strength lies in our collaborative approach, technical excellence, and ability to mobilise the right expertise at pace to support our clients’ requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Bridges Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At BakerHicks, our Bridges Team delivers expert engineering solutions across the full lifecycle of bridge and structures projects, from inspection and assessment through to design, refurbishment, strengthening, and replacement works. Our engineers work on a diverse portfolio of assets including highway bridges, railway bridges, footbridges, retaining structures, culverts, and other critical infrastructure across the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We combine technical excellence with a practical, collaborative approach, working closely with clients, asset owners, local authorities, contractors, and multidisciplinary teams to develop safe, sustainable, and cost-effective solutions. Our experience spans inspections, structural assessments, repair schemes, asset management programmes, and the delivery of complex infrastructure projects in highly regulated environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking Expressions of Interest from competent and experienced Bridge and Structural Inspectors to join our growing contractor talent pool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a live vacancy tied to a specific project. Instead, we are building a network of pre-qualified professionals who can be considered for assignments as needs arise across our infrastructure portfolio.&lt;br&gt;Applications are welcomed from anywhere in the UK. Site travel will normally be required, there is no requirement to be based near a BakerHicks office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are particularly keen to hear from inspectors based in Scotland, while welcoming applications from inspectors based in England.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome inspectors with experience in one or more of the following activities and environments:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Principal inspections, including close-up examination and access equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety, special and reactive inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspections for assessment and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Condition surveys (defect investigations and condition scoring)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highway structures on trunk road and local authority networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Railway structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspection and access planning, and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team leadership and technical review by appropriately qualified Senior Inspectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relevant asset types and construction forms may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Road and rail bridges, including footbridges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culverts and buried structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retaining walls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tunnel structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sign and signal gantries, masts and other ancillary highway structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structures over or adjacent to watercourses, including scour-related inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concrete, steel, masonry, timber, composite and post-tensioned structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants should be able to demonstrate the following, appropriate to the assignments sought:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant UK bridge or structures inspection experience, with a clear record of inspection roles and asset types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of applicable standards and client procedures, including NR/L3/CIV/006 and/or DMRB CS 450 where relevant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify, photograph and classify defects; record severity and extent; recognise urgent safety issues; and produce accurate reports and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to plan and coordinate inspection works, including access arrangements and traffic or rail control measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of structural materials, deterioration mechanisms, structural behaviour and inspection limitations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with National Highways, Transport Scotland, Network Rail, local authorities or comparable asset owners and supply chains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience producing inspection reports and condition assessments, including reporting using Bridge Condition Indicators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IT Literacy – proficient in the use of Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the assignment, the following will be required or advantageous:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current Bridge Inspector Certification Scheme (BICS) certification at Inspector or Senior Inspector level, appropriate to the work. Required where mandated by the client, including relevant Transport Scotland assignments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant BEng/MEng in civil or structural engineering qualification, or equivalent inspection experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current working-at-height and confined-space competence, where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IPAF/MEWP, IRATA rope-access, PASMA mobile access towers, Ladder or other relevant access qualifications, where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current Safe Working Near Water (SWNW) or other equivalent competence, where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current Safe use of Trolley Equipment or Rail Trolley controller, where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid CSCS or other required site-access certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For rail work, current Personal Track Safety (PTS) and other role-specific competences; SSSTS or SMSTS for supervisory duties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network Rail Competencies STE2 – 7 as defined in NR/SP/CTM/017&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Register Your Interest?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining our contractor talent pool, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be considered for assignments matching your competence, location and availability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a working relationship with BakerHicks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside experienced infrastructure professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support projects across a variety of sectors, clients and UK locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to Register Your Interest&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please submit your CV. Our Talent Acquisition team will review applications alongside our Infrastructure discipline leaders, and suitable candidates will be invited to an introductory discussion.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contract opportunities (Inside IR35 / PAYE engagement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working depending on project requirements (office/site/hybrid)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Locations across the UK&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Many of the positions within our company are subject to security clearance or security assurance levels.&amp;nbsp;The successful candidate must be able to obtain and maintain the appropriate level of security clearance or assurance level for this role, in line with client and sector requirements.&amp;nbsp;In some cases, additional nationality or residency criteria may also apply due to specific client or national security obligations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Further information on National security clearance levels can be found on the UK Government website: (&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/united-kingdom-security-vetting-clearance-levels/national-security-vetting-clearance-levels&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;National security vetting: clearance levels - GOV.UK&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About BakerHicks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve been innovating in design, engineering and project delivery since 1957 and operate from 14 locations for a truly European reach. For more about our company story, see:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://bakerhicks.com/en/about&quot;&gt;About | BakerHicks&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BakerHicks. A&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.morgansindall.com/&quot;&gt;Morgan Sindall Group&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;company.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whatever your discipline, you’ll be alongside some of the most talented people in the industry. Our network of offices are appealing, friendly and comfortable spaces, easily accessible by car or public transport. And our salary and benefits packages are some of the best in the industry.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BakerHicks is an equal opportunity employer. We care about creating an inclusive atmosphere and are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion throughout.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;BakerHicks is an inclusive organisation welcoming talent from all backgrounds. Applicants are assessed on the basis of personal merit and qualifications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Re-architecting Engineering for the Age of Intelligence&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;PhysicsX is the physics AI company for industrials. The company’s mission is to accelerate hardware innovation by overhauling what industrial engineering and manufacturing look like today. PhysicsX is building a new simulation software stack to deliver deep physics AI enablement across the entire engineering lifecycle. The company partners with leading organisations in aerospace &amp;amp; defence, automotive, semiconductors, materials, and energy &amp;amp; renewables, supporting them on some of their most critical and complex challenges. PhysicsX is headquartered in the United Kingdom, with offices in London, New York, and Singapore and an expanding presence in the Bay Area.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our simulation engineers and research scientists to develop an understanding of the physics and engineering challenges we are solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work at the intersection of data science and software engineering to transform prototype implementations to robust production-grade model implementations, libraries and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with multi-GPU/multi-node distributed systems for training and inference at the scale of PBs of data and hundreds of GPUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize the models and pipelines on all levels, from job scheduling down to GPU kernels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build scalable and robust infrastructure for end-to-end machine learning applications on cloud (CoreWeave, AWS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously apply and improve engineering best practices and standards, coach your colleagues in their adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm about using machine learning for science and engineering, and especially in scaling such solutions to real-world settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work autonomously in a fast-paced environment, learn and adapt quickly, scope, plan and deliver effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration and communication skills, especially with research scientists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with software engineering concepts and best practices (e.g., versioning, testing, CI/CD, API design, MLOps)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building ML models and pipelines in Python, using common libraries and frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the GPU programming ecosystem, ability to optimise models on all levels of the stack, going down to the level of CUDA/Triton/Warp kernels when necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience training and serving ML models at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale data processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;Nice to have&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain knowledge in physics and/or numerical methods, especially CFD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in the domain of ML for science or engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building infrastructure on cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP, CoreWeave)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with C/C++, especially for computer vision, geometry processing and scientific computing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build what actually matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help shape an AI-native engineering company at a formative stage, tackling problems that genuinely matter for industry and society. This is work with real-world impact - and something you can be proud to stand behind.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn alongside exceptional people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with a high-caliber, collaborative team of engineers, scientists, and operators who care deeply about doing great work, and about helping each other get better. We come from diverse backgrounds, but we share a commitment to operating at the highest level and addressing some of the most complex challenges out there. If you’re ambitious, thoughtful, and driven by impact, you’ll feel at home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence over hierarchy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate with a flat structure: good ideas win&amp;nbsp;- wherever they come from. Questioning assumptions and challenging the status quo isn’t just welcomed, it’s expected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sustainable pace, long-term ambition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building meaningful technology is a marathon, not a sprint. We believe in balancing focused, ambitious work with a life beyond it. Our hybrid model blends time together in our Shoreditch office with work-from-home days, giving you the flexibility to work sustainably while staying connected in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And it doesn’t stop there …&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Equity options&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- share meaningfully in the company you’re helping to build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏦&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;10% employer pension contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- because investing in future matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍽️&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Free office lunches&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- to keep you energised and focused.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👶&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Enhanced parental leave&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- 3 months full pay paternity and 6 months full pay maternity leave, to provide extra flexibility during the moments that matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍼&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;YellowNest nursery scheme&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- to help working parents manage childcare costs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;☀️&amp;nbsp;25 days of Annual Leave (+ Public Holidays)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;- because taking time to rest matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏥&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Private medical insurance&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- 100% employee cover, giving you complete peace of mind.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Wellhub Subscription&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;- gain access to thousands of gyms, classes and wellness apps, supporting both physical and mental wellbeing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👀&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Eye tests&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- because good work depends on good health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Personal development&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- dedicated support for learning, development, and leveling up over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💛&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Assistance Programme (EAP)&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- confidential wellbeing support, available whenever you need it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚲&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Bike2Work scheme and&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;🚆&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Season ticket loan&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- to make getting to work easier and greener.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚗&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Octopus EV salary sacrifice&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- for a simpler, more sustainable way to drive electric.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;🔎&amp;nbsp;Watch this space, we’re continuing to build this as we grow…&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We value diversity and are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of sex, race, religion, ethnicity, nationality, disability, age, sexual orientation or gender identity. We strongly encourage individuals from groups traditionally underrepresented in tech to apply. To help make a change, we sponsor bright women from disadvantaged backgrounds through their university degrees in science and mathematics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We collect diversity and inclusion data solely for the purpose of monitoring the effectiveness of our equal opportunities policies and ensuring compliance with employment and equality legislation. This information is confidential, used only in aggregate form, and will not influence the outcome of your application.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
